---
import LegalLayout from '@/layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/lib/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  path="/accessibility"
  eyebrow="Accessibility"
  heading="Accessibility statement"
  lede="STARS Academy wants every family, partner and job seeker to be able to use this website."
  description="STARS Academy's commitment to website accessibility, the standards we follow, and how to report a barrier."
>
  <h2>Our commitment</h2>
  <p>
    We designed this website to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2, Level AA. That includes:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Text and interface colors with sufficient contrast.</li>
    <li>Full keyboard navigation, with visible focus indicators.</li>
    <li>Page structure, headings and labels that work with screen readers.</li>
    <li>Forms with clear labels, instructions and error messages.</li>
    <li>Layouts that adapt to phones, tablets, desktop and browser zoom up to 400%.</li>
    <li>Reduced motion for visitors who prefer it.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Ongoing work</h2>
  <p>
    Accessibility is ongoing. We test new content as it is added and review the site regularly. Some linked content hosted by
    other services (such as our secure application forms) may not be fully within our control.
  </p>

  <h2>Tell us about a barrier</h2>
  <p>
    If anything on this site is difficult to use, please call us at <a href={SITE.phoneHref}>{SITE.phone}</a> or use our
    <a href="/contact-us">contact form</a>. We’ll work to provide the information you need in a format that works for you.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
